      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm taking the Eurostar from St Pancras to Paris next week. What are the current rules for luggage weight and how much time do I actually need to get to the platform for check-in?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the Eurostar, the luggage rules are quite flexible, but you should keep your baggage manageable, as you don't need to check it in like a flight. It's generally advised to have your main luggage sized to fit in the overhead racks or in the designated luggage areas at the end of the carriages. For the journey from St Pancras to Paris, you should aim to arrive at the station with plenty of time, ideally at least 45 minutes before your scheduled departure. This buffer time is crucial for navigating the station, finding your platform, and getting settled before the train starts moving.",
