    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i'm just worried about getting lost in all the tunnels and stairs. it feels like a bit of a maze in there. is there a specific part of the station that's the most tricky to get through?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The tunnels and stairs can certainly feel like a maze, and it's easy to get turned around, especially when you're distracted by the sheer volume of people. Trying to navigate the underground sections when you're rushing is where most people get lost, which is a common pitfall. It's a bit like trying to find a specific spot in a massive, sprawling underground network of old, interconnected tunnels, which is what some of the more complex areas feel like.\n\nIf you're concerned about getting lost, try to stick close to the main signage pointing towards the Eurostar platforms. Don't try to cut through every side passage; follow the main, well-lit arteries, as those are usually the most direct routes. Remember, even the most seasoned travelers sometimes need a moment to orient themselves in such a large space.",
